---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Gallery title="Pattern: multi-step wizard">
  <p class="demo-note">
    <strong>Who uses it</strong>: whoever is creating something too long for
    one screen, guided rather than dropped into a form — most often a
    first-time or occasional flow. <strong>What "done" looks like</strong>:
    every step completed or explicitly skippable, submitted once, and
    resumable if abandoned partway. A real multi-<em>step</em> flow — one
    panel visible at a time, Back/Next move
    between them — as opposed to <a href={base + '/patterns/detail-form'}>detail form</a>'s
    multi-<em>section</em> single screen. Composed from the existing
    <code>.bo-stepper</code> progress indicator plus a new opt-in behavior,
    <code>initWizard()</code>, that keeps the stepper and the visible panel in sync
    and moves focus to each new panel — the panels themselves are plain
    <code>.bo-form-section</code> fieldsets, nothing new to learn there.
    <strong>Not for a routine single-step task</strong> — if there is nothing
    to walk someone through, a wizard's Back/Next scaffolding is friction with
    no payoff; use a plain <a href={base + '/patterns/detail-form'}>detail
    form</a> instead. Its Next/Submit pair is the one legitimate
    two-primary-action layout in this system precisely because it exists to
    gate a guided multi-step flow, not a single screen.
  </p>
  <section class="demo">
    <div data-wizard data-wizard-current="0">
      <ol class="bo-stepper" role="list" style="max-inline-size: 40rem">
        <li class="bo-stepper__step" aria-current="step">
          <span class="bo-stepper__marker">1</span>
          <span class="bo-stepper__label">Vendor</span>
        </li>
        <li class="bo-stepper__step">
          <span class="bo-stepper__marker">2</span>
          <span class="bo-stepper__label">Line items</span>
        </li>
        <li class="bo-stepper__step">
          <span class="bo-stepper__marker">3</span>
          <span class="bo-stepper__label">Review</span>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div data-wizard-panel>
        <fieldset class="bo-form-section">
          <legend class="bo-form-section__legend">Vendor</legend>
          <div class="bo-form-row">
            <div class="bo-form-field">
              <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="wz-vendor">Vendor</label>
              <input class="bo-input" id="wz-vendor" value="Acme Supply Co." />
            </div>
            <div class="bo-form-field">
              <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="wz-terms">Terms</label>
              <select class="bo-select" id="wz-terms"><option>Net 30</option><option>Net 60</option></select>
            </div>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
      </div>
      <div data-wizard-panel hidden>
        <fieldset class="bo-form-section">
          <legend class="bo-form-section__legend">Line items</legend>
          <div class="bo-form-row">
            <div class="bo-form-field">
              <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="wz-item">Item</label>
              <input class="bo-input" id="wz-item" value="SKU-3391 · Standing desk" />
            </div>
            <div class="bo-form-field">
              <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="wz-qty">Qty</label>
              <input class="bo-input bo-input--numeric" id="wz-qty" value="4" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
      </div>
      <div data-wizard-panel hidden>
        <fieldset class="bo-form-section">
          <legend class="bo-form-section__legend">Review</legend>
          <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Everything above, read-only, before submitting.</p>
        </fieldset>
      </div>

      <div class="bo-form-actions">
        <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary" type="button" data-wizard-back>Back</button>
        <button class="bo-btn" type="button" data-wizard-next>Next</button>
        <button class="bo-btn" type="submit" data-wizard-submit hidden>Submit</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted"><strong>Wizards require <code>initWizard()</code></strong> —
      wired below. Panels 2+ carry a static <code>hidden</code> attribute, so
      without it they stay hidden rather than all rendering at once — but
      Back/Next never fire and Submit never un-hides, so the wizard cannot be
      completed. See the States table's "No JS" row.</p>
  </section>
  <script>
    import { initWizard } from '@busy-office/ui/js';
    initWizard();
  </script>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Anatomy</h2>
    <ol class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight docs-list">
      <li><strong>Stepper</strong> — where you are, what is done, what is
      left. <span class="bo-u-text-muted">Not in this demo: clicking a
      completed step to jump back. `initWizard()` only wires Back/Next
      today; the markers here are plain, not buttons.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Step panel</strong> — one form per step, each independently valid.</li>
      <li><strong>Footer navigation</strong> &mdash; Back / Next, with Next as the form&rsquo;s submit so Enter works.</li>
      <li><strong>Resume affordance</strong> — a wizard nobody can resume is a wizard people abandon.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Data contract</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Returns / on failure</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">POST /wizard/:id/step/:n</td><td>the NEXT step fragment on success; 422 → this step re-rendered with errors and values</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">GET /wizard/:id</td><td>resume at the furthest completed step</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">POST /wizard/:id/finish</td><td>the created record; wizard state is discarded server-side only after this succeeds</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>States</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">What ships</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Step invalid</td><td>stay on the step; focus the first invalid field — never advance and report later</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Partial persistence</td><td>each step posts as it completes, so a closed tab loses at most one step</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Back navigation</td><td>values preserved; going back must never clear later steps silently</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Abandoned / resumed</td><td>reopening lands on the furthest completed step with a note of what remains</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Final submit</td><td>disable the whole footer while posting — a double-submitted wizard creates two records</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cross-step validation</td><td>if step 3 invalidates step 1, say WHICH step and link back to it</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No JS</td><td>panels 2+ stay hidden (native <code>hidden</code>, not a JS toggle), so the form reads correctly, but Back/Next never fire and Submit never un-hides — the wizard cannot be completed</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Components used</h2>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted"><span class="bo-badge">complexity 3 of 4</span></p>
    <ul class="bo-cluster docs-list-bare">
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/stepper'}>Stepper</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/form'}>Forms</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/button'}>Button</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/patterns/validation-summary'}>Validation summary</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <Related links={[
    ["/components/stepper", "Stepper"],
    ["/components/form", "Forms"],
    ["/patterns/detail-form", "Detail form (multi-section, single screen)"],
  ]} />
</Gallery>
